\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2><$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Scene purpose\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 This is primarily a chance to see 
\f1\b \strokec2 Chilo, Kleo and Solo alone together
\f0\b0 \strokec2 .\
Elsewhere they tend to function as a unit inside other people\'92s stories. Here, they can stop being a three-headed oracle long enough for us to discover that they do not necessarily agree about what their own prophecy means or how current events should be interpreted.\
The scene should establish a 
\f1\b \strokec2 private fracture that already exists
\f0\b0 \strokec2 , so that the later Kebab behaviour\'97especially Chilo and Kleo pushing while Solo cautions\'97does not appear suddenly for plot convenience.\
But the fracture must remain interpretive rather than moral.\
They are not:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 destroy universe / save universe
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
They are closer to:\

\f1\b \strokec2 what do these events mean, and what are we entitled to do because of them?
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Setting\
